---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Epigraph from '../../components/Epigraph.astro';
import { identity } from '../../config/site';

/**
 * The Bengali section. Empty of posts today; the couplet is its content.
 *
 * The band under the masthead used to sit on /blog/, where it was a line the
 * site stands behind attached to a page of English essays. It belongs here:
 * "বিশ্বমানব হবি যদি / শাশ্বত বাঙ্গালী হ’॥" is the argument for the section
 * existing, so the section is where it goes. /blog/ no longer renders it, and
 * it is still rendered on exactly one page — see Epigraph.astro.
 *
 * Named in its own script. The heading is বাংলা, not "Bangla": romanising it
 * is the same move as the romanised "GURUSADAY DUTT" that was built under the
 * couplet and removed, which explained the line to a reader who cannot read it
 * and turned something the site means into an exhibit with a caption.
 *
 * The tab, though, is the Latin "BN", and that is not a compromise. Every
 * navigation link is `.label` — mono, uppercase, letter-spaced 0.18em — and
 * Bengali must never be letter-spaced, because the matra is one continuous
 * headstroke across a word and tracking cuts it into pieces. A Bengali nav
 * label would need the one class in the bar to opt out of the bar's own
 * treatment. `bn` is also the language's ISO 639-1 code, which is what the
 * `lang` attribute on the verse already says.
 *
 * WHAT THIS PAGE SAYS, and why it is not "Coming soon":
 *
 *   1. A page that only announces itself is a dead end. The empty-state
 *      guidance is unanimous on this — say what the space is for and leave a
 *      way onward — so the page states the purpose in one sentence and ends
 *      with the route to the writing that does exist.
 *   2. NN/g's homepage guidelines say not to post "under construction" for
 *      parts of a site yet to come. What makes this page not that is the
 *      couplet: there is something here to read, and it is the one thing on
 *      the site that could not have been written for anybody else.
 *   3. No date and no countdown. A promise with a month on it is a promise
 *      that goes stale by itself.
 *   4. No "notify me" field. It needs a third-party endpoint, which this site
 *      does not have and does not want — same reason there is no contact form.
 *      The blog's RSS already exists for anyone who wants to be told.
 *   5. **No `noindex`.** A placeholder is only thin content when it is a bare
 *      announcement; this one has real text, a real description and a real
 *      link, so it is indexable like every other page. The standard failure
 *      here is adding `noindex` "just for now" and forgetting it at launch,
 *      which is a section nobody can find on the day it fills up.
 *
 * Built like 404.astro rather than with <Section>: this is one short block,
 * not a list with a heading rail, and `.section__title` carries a positive
 * letter-spacing that must not touch Bengali.
 */
---

<Base
  title="বাংলা"
  description={`Writing in Bengali by ${identity.name}. Nothing is published here yet — the rest of the site's writing is in English.`}
  preloadBengali
>
  {
    /* Outside the block below on purpose: the band runs the full width of the
      viewport and belongs to the masthead above it. See Epigraph.astro. */
  }
  <Epigraph />

  <div class="shell bn">
    <h1 class="bn__title" lang="bn">বাংলা</h1>

    <p class="bn__body">
      Writing in Bengali will be published here. Everything on the site so far is in
      English.
    </p>

    <div class="bn__actions">
      <a href="/blog/" class="btn">The English writing</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .bn {
    padding-block: clamp(4rem, 2rem + 10vw, 10rem);
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  /* Three inherited properties have to be taken back off this heading, and all
     three are wrong for Bengali rather than merely different:

       letter-spacing — `h1` is tracked to -0.031em, tuned to Inter. Negative
       tracking on Bengali crowds the matra into the glyphs hanging under it,
       and the headstroke stops reading as one stroke.
       font-weight    — Tiro Bangla loads at 400 only. `font-synthesis-weight:
                        none` is global, so the inherited 600 silently returns
                        the regular anyway; asking for what exists is honest.
       line-height    — 1.15 is a Latin cap-height measure. Bengali stacks reph
                        and matra above the line and jophola below it. */
  .bn__title {
    font-family: var(--font-bengali);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: normal;
  }

  .bn__body {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    max-width: 48ch;
  }

  .bn__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
